    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d505">

                <pb facs="0518" n="434" xml:id="pg434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. No. 763.72112/3494</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-23T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 23, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 14, 11 a.m. Apparently no obstacle in law of United States to
                    commercial relations between Americans and Germans in China, but as a matter of
                    policy they should be discouraged. How extensive are such relations?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
